UPDATE companies SET description='Service Electric Cable TV & Communications traces its roots to 1948 in Mahanoy City, Pennsylvania, where John Walson Sr. (born John Walsonavich) invented cable television to bring broadcast signals to his appliance-store customers in the mountains. The company moved its headquarters to 2200 Avenue A in Bethlehem in 2014 and remains a third-generation, family-owned business now led by John M. Walson, grandson of the founder.

The company operates as a regional telecommunications provider delivering broadband internet (up to Gig+ speeds with eero whole-home WiFi), cable television with hundreds of channels including local sports networks such as the Service Electric Network (SEN) and SEN+ streaming app, and voice services. It also runs a dedicated business division — Service Electric Business — supplying internet, phone, and TV to small, medium, and enterprise customers with a promise of free local, same-day service calls. Service territory spans the Lehigh Valley, Hunterdon County (NJ), and Wilkes-Barre (PA).

Customers include residential subscribers and businesses across northeastern Pennsylvania and western New Jersey. Partnerships with PenTeleData and Alianza extend the portfolio to hosted voice and advanced broadband solutions.

The Walson family emphasizes community involvement and local ownership as differentiators: the company was the first in the nation to carry HBO (1972), a founding partner of the Lehigh Valley IronPigs and Phantoms, and operates the hyper-local Service Electric Network covering high school and collegiate sports, Musikfest, and regional news.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Broadband internet (up to Gig+ speeds)", "eero whole-home WiFi deployment", "Cable television (Full Basic, Broadband TV packages)", "Local sports and community network (SEN, SEN+ streaming app)", "Business voice services (hosted PBX, SIP trunking via Alianza)", "Managed business internet with static IPs and priority support", "Competitive Local Exchange Carrier (CLEC) telephone service"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Cable television", "Internet service provider", "Business communications", "Managed services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Third-generation family ownership since 1948", "Local, same-day service calls for business customers", "Hyper-local sports and community programming on SEN/SEN+", "Partnerships with PenTeleData and Alianza for hosted voice and broadband"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 by John Walson Sr. -> /about", "Headquarters consolidated to Bethlehem 2014 -> /about", "Third-generation family ownership (John M. Walson president since 2012) -> /about", "Services: Internet, Cable TV, Phone, Business communications -> /services, /", "Service areas: Lehigh Valley, Hunterdon, Wilkes-Barre -> /, /about, /services", "First cable company to offer HBO (1972) -> /about", "Service Electric Network (SEN) and SEN+ streaming app -> /, /about", "Partnerships with PenTeleData and Alianza -> /about", "CLEC status since 1998 -> /about", "Business division offers same-day local service calls -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Service Electric Business is a local leader in business communications services, offering Internet, phone, and cable TV with free local, same-day service calls.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='service-electric-cable-tv-communications-bethlehem-hq' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Service Metal Fabricators, based in Williamsburg, Virginia, has operated for over 40 years as a precision sheet metal fabricator.

The shop produces NEMA-rated enclosures, brackets, panels, assemblies, and stainless-steel medical containers. Its capabilities span shearing, CNC punching, press brake forming, vertical milling, CNC machining, MIG/TIG and spot welding, riveting, hardware insertion, silk screening, chemical finishing, powder coating, and painting. Operations run from a 12-acre campus with 56,000 to 60,000 square feet of manufacturing space, supported by a production workforce that includes three quality-assurance professionals for every 25 production employees.

Customers come from electronics, industrial equipment, diagnostic and measurement, medical, aerospace, military, TEMPEST computing, solar energy, and transportation sectors. Notable programs include enclosures for Becton Dickinson’s laboratory blood analyzers, chassis for a $15 billion transportation company’s electronics division, components for a solar smart-circuitry venture, and helm stations installed on the bridges of a dozen U.S. aircraft carriers.

The company differentiates itself through vertical integration that includes its own delivery fleet, offering free shipping within 200 miles, and machine redundancy to protect lead times. It also provides design engineering, design-for-manufacturability guidance, and reverse-engineering support, while maintaining adherence to military and industry standards such as AMS-STD-1595, MIL-DTL-5541, and RoHS.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO compliant','AMS-STD-1595','MIL-DTL-5541','RoHS Compliant','FED-STD-595','MS51835','NASM8846D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shearing", "CNC Punching", "Press Brake Forming", "Vertical Milling", "CNC Machining", "MIG Welding", "TIG Welding", "Spot Welding", "Riveting", "Mechanical Assembly", "Hardware Insertion", "Silk Screening", "Chemical Finishing", "Powder Coating", "Painting", "Prototyping", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "CNC Forming", "Engineering Services", "Plating", "Chromate Conversion Coating (MIL-DTL-5541)", "Quality Assurance", "Deburring", "Surface Graining"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Industrials", "Diagnostic/Measurement", "Medical", "Aerospace", "Military", "TEMPEST Computing", "Solar Energy", "Transportation"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Aluminum", "Steel"], "equipment": ["Strippit CNC Punch Presses (4)", "Haas Precision CNC Vertical Mills (3)", "Granite Inspection Tables", "Calipers", "Micrometers", "Digital Height Gauges", "Calibration Equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": ".002-.004 inch", "built_on": ["Own fleet of delivery trucks with free delivery within 200 miles", "Machine redundancy to ensure on-time delivery", "In-house QA staffing ratio of 3 professionals per 25 production workers", "Design engineering, DFM, and reverse-engineering assistance", "Adherence to military and industry standards (AMS-STD-1595, MIL-DTL-5541, RoHS)"], "facts_used": ["Williamsburg, Virginia location -> /", "Over 40 years in business -> /", "Facility size 12-acre, 56,000 sq ft -> /", "Facility size 60,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Industries served (electronics, industrials, diagnostic/measurement, medical, aerospace, military, TEMPEST, solar, transportation) -> /, /about-us", "Specific customers: Becton Dickinson, $15B transportation company, solar company, U.S. aircraft carriers -> /about-us", "Capabilities list (shearing, CNC punching, forming, milling, welding, assembly, finishing, etc.) -> /services", "Equipment: 4 Strippit CNC Punch Presses, 3 Haas CNC Vertical Mills -> /quality", "Certifications: ISO compliant, AMS-STD-1595, MIL-DTL-5541, RoHS, FED-STD-595, MS51835, NASM8846D -> /quality", "Tolerances .002-.004 inch for punch presses -> /quality", "Vertical integration with own delivery fleet, free delivery within 200 miles -> /", "QA ratio 3 per 25 production staff -> /quality", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, steel -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Service Metal Fabricators is a one-stop shop providing comprehensive precision sheet metal fabrication services for over 40 years.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='service-metal-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Seven Trees Woodworking is based in New Holland, Pennsylvania, and was founded in 2009 by Jarin Smoker. Smoker’s long‑standing passion for fine millwork led him to start the company, which has since grown into a team of skilled craftsmen dedicated to turning raw wood into finished architectural pieces.

The shop produces architectural millwork, custom cabinetry, custom doors, commercial millwork, private‑label and white‑label furniture, and metalwork. Operations run from a facility on King Court, where the team handles projects ranging from residential cabinetry to large‑scale commercial installations for restaurants and hotels.

Primary markets include the restaurant and hospitality sectors, as well as commercial, residential, and furniture‑brand clients. The company has supplied private‑label furniture for international brands and regularly works with architects and designers on custom projects for hotels, offices, and homes.

Seven Trees emphasizes a willingness to take on challenging projects that other shops decline, positioning itself as a problem‑solver for complex millwork and furniture requirements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural millwork", "Custom cabinetry", "Custom doors", "Commercial millwork", "Private label furniture", "White label furniture", "Metalwork", "CNC machining"], "industries": ["Restaurant", "Hospitality", "Commercial", "Residential", "Furniture"], "materials": ["Wood", "Metal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom millwork for restaurants, hotels, homes, and offices", "Private\u2011label furniture for international brands", "Willingness to tackle challenging projects others decline", "In\u2011house metalwork capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 by Jarin Smoker -> db", "Headquarters New Holland, Pennsylvania -> db", "Services: architectural millwork, custom cabinetry, custom doors, commercial millwork, private label furniture, white label furniture, metalwork -> page /", "Industries served: restaurant, hospitality, commercial, residential, furniture -> page /", "Private label furniture for international brands -> page /", "Team of skilled craftsmen -> db", "Website seventrees.com -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "turning raw wood into beautiful millwork pieces", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/seven-trees-woodworking/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='seven-trees-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Severance Foods operates from Hartford, Connecticut, where it was founded in 1985 by three former Heublein food scientists — Richard Stevens, John Grikis, and Rich Dana. After R.J. Reynolds acquired Heublein in 1984, the trio used their severance packages to acquire a facility and equipment, launching a company to meet the Northeast''s growing demand for tortillas and tortilla chips. The business remains family-owned and operated under the Pan De Oro brand.

The company manufactures tortilla chips and salsa under its own Pan De Oro label and provides co-packing services for other brands. Production emphasizes non-GMO, organic, and hand-crafted methods. The plant in Hartford is described as the largest tortilla chip manufacturer and co-packer in the Northeast, though specific facility size, headcount, and volume figures are not disclosed.

Customers include restaurants, schools, concession operators, and retail grocery stores across New York, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania, as well as farmers markets throughout the region. The co-packing side serves other food brands seeking a regional production partner.

The founders started the business after their work on Ortega Mexican Foods at Heublein revealed an unmet need for Mexican-style products in the Northeast. They cite attention to high-quality standards, all-natural ingredients, and unique flavor development as the reasons their chips have gained traction since 1985.', certifications=ARRAY['Non-GMO','Organic']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tortilla chip manufacturing", "Salsa production", "Co-packing", "Product development", "Quality assurance", "Non-GMO production", "Organic production"], "industries": ["Food service", "Restaurants", "Schools", "Concessions", "Retail grocery", "Farmers markets", "Co-packing for food brands"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1985", "Largest tortilla chip manufacturer and co-packer in the Northeast", "Non-GMO and organic certified products", "Hand-crafted with all-natural ingredients", "Co-packing services for other brands"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 by Richard Stevens, John Grikis, Rich Dana -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Headquarters: 3478 Main Street, Hartford, CT -> /", "Largest manufacturer and co-packer of tortilla chips in the Northeast -> /about", "Products: tortilla chips and salsa under Pan De Oro brand -> /", "Non-GMO, organic, hand-crafted -> /", "Serves restaurants, schools, concessions -> /about", "Co-packing services for other brands -> /about", "Retail presence in NY, NJ, PA and farmers markets -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Severance Foods is the largest manufacturer and co-packer of tortilla chips in the northeast.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pan-de-oro-tortilla-chip-company/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='severance-foods-pan-de-oro' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Shaker Furniture of Maine operates from a two-floor, nearly 10,000-square-foot showroom on Route 1 in Scarborough, Maine. The business is owned by proprietor Steve Celona, who emphasizes that every piece is solid wood and made with pride in American shops.

The company manufactures and sells solid-wood furniture including bedroom sets, living-room pieces, dining tables and chairs, and accent items. Materials are native hardwoods such as cherry, maple, and oak, along with classic pine offered prefinished or ready for paint or stain. The facility supports custom builds to customer specifications, and the company ships nationwide.

The brand differentiates itself with a “Proudly Made in Maine and Made in America” commitment, highlighting domestic production, timeless Shaker-inspired designs, and a hands-on shopping experience across two floors of inventory.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Custom furniture building", "Wood finishing (prefinished or ready for paint/stain)", "Nationwide shipping", "Retail showroom"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Cherry", "Maple", "Oak", "Pine"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proudly Made in Maine and Made in America", "Custom-build to your specifications", "Nationwide shipping", "Two-floor showroom with nearly 10,000 sq ft of inventory"], "facts_used": ["Location: Scarborough, Maine -> /", "Facility: two floors, nearly 10,000 sq ft -> /", "Proprietor: Steve Celona -> /", "Products: solid wood furniture (bedroom, living room, dining, accent) -> /", "Materials: cherry, maple, oak, pine -> /", "Custom building available -> /", "Ships nationwide -> /", "Made in Maine/Made in America claim -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every single piece is solid wood, and made with pride in American shops.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='shaker-furniture-of-maine' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sheet Metal Enterprises operates from Dedham, Massachusetts, on the Boston-Dedham line near I-95. The company has been in business for more than a decade, positioned minutes from local HVAC supply houses.

The shop specializes in custom-fabricated HVAC ductwork and fittings, producing ducts in standard 4-foot and 8-foot lengths as well as precise custom sizes such as 74 3/4 inches. Beyond ductwork, it manufactures copper shower pans and other sheet metal products, including soldering brass strainers into the pans. The operation emphasizes quick turnaround for a custom fabrication facility.

The company''s proximity to supply houses and its job-site delivery service support contractors who need accurately sized ductwork on tight schedules.

Ed''s field background informs the company''s approach: he guides customers on sizing and duct design, offering practical installation insights. The business was built to make the procurement and installation process smoother, combining custom fabrication with direct delivery to the job site.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom HVAC ductwork fabrication", "Custom duct fitting fabrication", "Copper shower pan fabrication", "Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Soldering of brass fittings", "Custom length cutting", "Job-site delivery"], "industries": ["HVAC", "Plumbing", "Residential construction", "Commercial construction"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Copper", "Brass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fast turnaround for custom fabrication", "Custom ductwork cut to exact lengths (e.g., 74 3/4\")", "Job-site delivery service", "Owner''s 30 years HVAC and fabrication experience", "Field installation expertise guiding design and sizing"], "facts_used": ["Family operated business located on Boston/Dedham line -> /", "Conveniently located near I-95 -> /", "Delivery service drops off at job site -> /", "Specializes in custom sized ductwork and fittings -> /", "Ducts come in 4ft or 8ft lengths, custom lengths available -> /", "Makes copper shower pans and other custom sheet metal products -> /", "Solders brass strainers into copper pans -> /", "Custom fabrication shop specializing in HVAC duct work and copper pans -> /about", "In business for over 10 years -> /about", "Located in Dedham minutes from HVAC supply houses -> /about", "Fast turnaround for custom fabrication shop -> /about", "Owner Ed has over 30 years experience in HVAC and fabrication -> /about", "Ed worked 22 years installing HVAC equipment for residential and commercial buildings -> /about", "Expertise in sizing and duct work design -> /about", "Headquarters in Dedham, Massachusetts -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sheet Metal Enterprises is a custom fabrication shop that specializes in hvac duct work and copper pans.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sheet-metal-enterprises' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SiCamore Semi operates a pure-play semiconductor foundry in Bend, Oregon. The company describes itself as a U.S.-based boutique foundry with three decades of experience in wafer fabrication, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The foundry specializes in high-power, high-voltage wide-bandgap devices using silicon carbide (SiC) and gallium nitride (GaN) on 100 mm and 150 mm wafers. Its process flow covers photolithography with ASML 5000 I-line steppers and Karl Suss aligners, thin-film deposition (sputtering, PVD, CVD, PECVD, e-beam evaporation), frontside and backside metallization, thermal oxidation and diffusion, wet and dry etching (RIE), rapid thermal annealing, and ion implantation (cold and hot). SiC-specific steps include high-temperature implant and anneal, gate oxidation with nitric oxide anneal, and a dedicated gold wafer fab for high-reliability, radiation-hardened, and RF devices. Additional partner services encompass device design, wafer thinning, dicing, packaging, and test.

SiCamore serves electric-vehicle, medical, industrial, aerospace and defense, and academic customers. It supplies SiC diodes, MOSFETs, JBSFETs, JFETs, IGBTs, and Si SGTOs/SDIODEs for industrial power and switching applications. The company also collaborates with universities on NASA, NSF, DOE, and DOD grants focused on space, grid, weapons, EV, data-center, and communications technologies, and it targets U.S. military, intelligence, and government agencies alongside commercial transportation, telecommunications, and healthcare infrastructure markets.

The company states its mission is to deliver innovative power-semiconductor solutions through the development of silicon and wide-bandgap technologies. It aims to become the power-semiconductor facility in the U.S. Northwest for advanced wide-bandgap device fabrication, integration, and testing, emphasizing a stable, ITAR-certified environment for aerospace and defense programs.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["100 mm & 150 mm wafer production for Si and SiC", "Single-step foundry device manufacturing", "Multi-project wafer (MPW) service", "Dedicated gold (Au) wafer fab", "Wafer probe with Keysight B1505A power device analyzer", "Photolithography (ASML 5000 I-line steppers, Karl Suss aligners)", "Thin film deposition (sputtering, PVD, CVD, PECVD, e-beam evaporation)", "Frontside/backside metal deposition (Ti/TiW/AlCu, Ti/Ni/Ag, Ti/Pt/Au, AlSiCu)", "Thermal oxidation and diffusion (Thermco, MRL)", "Wet chemical etch", "Plasma dry etch", "RIE etch", "Rapid thermal annealing (RTA)", "Ion implantation (cold and hot)", "SiC single-step process", "High-temperature implant and anneal", "Gate oxidation with nitric oxide anneal", "Gold wafer fab for HiRel/Rad Hard/RF", "Device design", "Wafer thinning", "Wafer dicing", "Packaging and test"], "industries": ["Electric Vehicles", "Medical", "Industrial", "Aerospace & Defense", "Academia", "Transportation", "Telecommunications", "Healthcare infrastructure"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", "Gold", "Titanium", "Tungsten", "Aluminum Copper", "Nickel", "Silver", "Platinum"], "equipment": ["ASML 5000 I-line steppers", "Karl Suss aligners", "Thermco oxidation/diffusion furnaces", "MRL oxidation/diffusion furnaces", "Keysight B1505A power device analyzer/curve tracer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pure-play foundry for advanced materials and power semiconductors", "ITAR-certified secure environment for aerospace and defense