UPDATE companies SET description='Silver State Wire & Cable Inc. began in 1991 in Sparks, Nevada, as a woman‑owned small business. It started as a modest value‑added service provider with two employees and three 1950s‑era wire processing machines, cutting and kitting wire, cable, and tubing for local assembly houses and OEMs.

Today the company provides wire processing, cable assembly, wiring harness fabrication, crimping, and electronic component testing, along with supply‑chain services such as kitting and just‑in‑time delivery. It also manufactures proprietary products including the Lacing Tape Dispenser, BRAIDLITE™ lightweight braided shielding for space applications, and the SumiMark IV Plus thermal‑transfer marking system. The operation serves programs ranging from hobby aircraft to satellites and fighter jets.

Silver State’s customer base spans aerospace, space, defense, and general aviation. Clients include OEMs building satellites, prime contractors rewiring fighter jets, and smaller shops assembling experimental aircraft.

