UPDATE companies SET description='Southern Motion was founded in 1996 in Pontotoc, Mississippi, by Guy Lipscomb and his wife Sandy. The couple named the company after a painting titled "Southern Motion" they discovered while shopping, which captured the spirit of relaxation and comfort they wanted to build into their furniture. From the start, the goal was singular: manufacture only reclining furniture and make it better than anyone else had.

Today the company operates five facilities in northern Mississippi and employs more than 1,500 workers. Its product line spans sofas, sectionals, recliners, and accent chairs equipped with features such as power headrests, massage and heat systems (branded SoCozi™), wireless charging, wall-hugger mechanisms, and swivel-glider bases. The furniture is marketed as American-made with both domestic and imported components.

Southern Motion sells through a network of independent retailers across the United States, Canada, and Mexico.

Leadership emphasizes that American workers can produce a quality, competitively priced product, and the brand positions itself as a design and innovation leader in the motion-furniture category. Community involvement, including long-term support for the American Cancer Society''s Relay for Life and other local charities, is also highlighted as part of the company''s identity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Reclining furniture manufacturing", "Power mechanism integration (headrest, lumbar, recline)", "Massage and heat system integration (SoCozi\u2122)", "Wireless charging integration", "Wall-hugger mechanism design", "Swivel and glider mechanism assembly", "Upholstery and sewing", "Foam fabrication (Energex cushion)", "Wood frame construction", "Design and innovation of motion furniture"], "industries": ["Furniture", "Home furnishings", "Retail furniture"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 in Pontotoc, Mississippi -> /about-us", "Founders: Guy Lipscomb and his wife Sandy -> /about-us", "Company named after painting ''Southern Motion'' -> /about-us", "Initial focus: manufacture only reclining furniture -> /about-us", "Currently employs over 1,500 workers in five Mississippi-based facilities -> /about-us", "Products include sofas, sectionals, recliners, accent chairs with power headrest, massage & heat, wireless charging, wall hugger, swivel glider -> /", "Sells through independent retailers in US, Canada, Mexico -> /", "Marketed as American Made Furniture with Domestic and Imported Parts -> /", "Believes American workers can manufacture quality, competitively priced product -> /about-us", "Leader in design and innovation in motion furniture -> /about-us", "Community involvement: Relay for Life, I AM ALS, CASA, Salvation Army, Night to Shine, Crossroads Ranch -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evid