UPDATE companies SET description='Standex Electronics is headquartered in Fairfield, Ohio. The company describes its origins as a single precision manufacturing operation that evolved into a diversified global platform through strategic acquisitions and organic growth. Today it operates as the parent company for three specialized divisions: Standex Detect, Standex Edge, and Standex Grid.

The company designs and manufactures precision-engineered electronic components across its three divisions. Standex Detect produces reed switches, relays, and sensors for automation, transportation, test and measurement, and energy applications. Standex Edge delivers custom magnetics including planar transformers, inductors, chokes, and EMI components for power conversion in industrial, medical, military, and aerospace markets. Standex Grid supplies low- and medium-voltage instrument transformers, bushings, and related products for grid reliability and power delivery. Operations span manufacturing facilities, design centers, and sales offices across North America, Europe, and Asia, enabling rapid prototyping and vertically integrated production.

Standex serves a broad range of industries including automotive (passenger, commercial, off-road, construction, agriculture), aerospace and military, medical, renewable and alternative energy, telecommunications, industrial equipment, smart home, transportation, and electrical utilities. Customers include OEMs and utility companies requiring mission-critical components for switch-mode power supplies, grid infrastructure, and sensing applications.

The company emphasizes its deep vertical integration as a differentiator, stating it allows consistent quality, rapid prototyping, and innovative design tailored to demanding applications. Its engineer-to-engineer collaborative approach — structured as Innovate, Consult, Engineer, Deliver — is rooted in customer intimacy and backed by a global footprint that provides local expertise with global resources.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom engineered electronic component design", "Off-the-shelf component portfolio", "Reed switch manufacturing", "Relay manufacturing", "Sensor manufacturing", "Planar transformer design and manufacturing", "Inductor and choke manufacturing", "EMI component manufacturing", "Low-voltage instrument transformer manufacturing", "Medium-voltage instrument transformer manufacturing", "Bushing manufacturing", "Rapid prototyping", "Power magnetics design", "Switching and sensing technology development", "Grid solution engineering"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aerospace", "Military and Defense", "Medical", "Energy", "Industrial", "Renewable Energy", "Telecommunications", "Smart Home", "Transportation", "Electrical Utilities", "Test and Measurement"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Deep vertical integration for consistent quality and rapid prototyping", "Global footprint with manufacturing, design, and sales across North America, Europe, and Asia", "Engineer-to-engineer collaborative methodology (Innovate, Consult, Engineer, Deliver)", "Three complementary divisions covering switching/sensing, magnetics, and grid solutions", "Decades of expertise from pioneering reed switches to advanced magnetics and power solutions"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fairfield, Ohio -> db", "Three divisions: Standex Detect, Standex Edge, Standex Grid -> /about", "Products: reed switches, relays, sensors, transformers, inductors, planar magnetics, instrument transformers, bushings -> /about, /", "Global operations across North America, Europe, Asia -> /about", "Industries served: automotive, aerospace, medical, energy, industrial, military, renewable energy, telecommunications, smart home, transportation, utilities -> /about, /, industries_served", "Vertical integration for quality and rapid prototyping -> /about", "Engineer-to-engineer approach: Innovate, Consult, Engineer, Deliver -> /about", "Design and manufacture of precision-engineered electronic components -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Standex Electronics is a global leader in the design and manufacture of precision-engineered electronic components", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='standex-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1946, State Fabricators Inc. (StateFab) has remained in Farmington Hills, Michigan, growing from a 1,900-square-foot startup to a 26,000-square-foot production welding shop on a seven-acre campus with overhead crane capacity.

The company focuses on custom steel fabrication for automotive conveyor systems, building carriers, skillets, line platforms, robot gantries, and custom assemblies. Its 50-plus fixture builders, certified welders, and operators run jobs from one-off prototypes to thousand-unit runs. Every subassembly passes through a final checking fixture so that a five-pound bracket and a five-thousand-pound carrier leave the floor with the same repeatability. The facility includes 26,000 square feet under crane and seven acres for staging large fabrications such as line platforms and robot gantries.

StateFab is a long-time Tier One and Tier Two supplier to the automotive industry, providing overhead, inverted, skillet, ELPO, paint, door, and cab carrier systems to plants across North America.

