ship_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='stitch-kentucky-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Stone Enterprises Inc. is based in Omaha, Nebraska. The company traces its roots to February 2000, when it acquired a small machine shop in Hastings, Nebraska, to produce two components for a food‑processing distributor. Recognizing broader demand, the owners expanded by purchasing a parts distributor in 2002 and adding a CNC machine shop to begin custom fabrication. A full‑time design engineer joined in 2007, and the 2010 acquisition of American Meat Equipment solidified the firm’s focus on food‑processing equipment and replacement parts.

Today Stone Enterprises manufactures both custom machinery and a wide range of replacement parts. Its equipment line includes the Stone Chine Saw, Hot Dog Peeler, Vacuum Table, Dip Tank Conveyor, Custom Sinks, Crossover Stairs, and Rotary Screen Filter. The replacement‑parts portfolio covers brands such as Handtmann, Ross, Townsend, Kartridg Pak, KP CHUB, Marel, Multivac, and others. Operations are carried out by a team of 35 — three design engineers, nine fabricators, ten master machinists, and twelve support staff — working from a facility that houses CNC machining, fabrication, and assembly capabilities.

Its customers include meat and poultry plants, prepared‑foods facilities, and packaging operations that rely on equipment from the OEMs listed above. Stone Enterprises positions itself as a cost‑saving alternative to original‑equipment manufacturers, offering parts that meet or exceed OEM specifications.

